            <ArticleTitle>Ochronotic cardiovascular disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>441-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ochronosis is a disease of tyrosine metabolism. Although most commonly associated with alcaptonuria and spondyloarthropathy, cardiovascular abnormalities have been associated. We describe a case which exemplifies the cardiovascular findings in this entity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
